    "text": "Two players MAX and MIN alternate turns in this unit’s examples. Zero-sum utility Every value uses MAX’s perspective; MIN prefers lower values. Deterministic transitions A legal action has one specified successor. Perfect information The current game state is observable to both players. Full-tree guarantees also require a finite game tree or correct handling of repetitions and draws.",
    "notes": "Zero-sum means U_MIN=−U_MAX, or an equivalent constant-sum normalization. Alternating turns simplify the presentation; a general implementation should ask the state who acts next rather than blindly flipping at every recursive call. Perfect information concerns observations of the game state. It does not require reading an opponent’s private intentions or plans."
